Actually, let me reconsider the `uri_decoder` function. When `*s == '%'`, it reads `s[1]` and `s[2]`. If `s` is at `end-1` (last char), then `s[1]` and `s[2]` are out of bounds. But the buffer is `g_malloc(length+1)`, so `s[1]` when `s=end-1` reads at `end` which is within the allocated `length+1` buffer (the nul terminator position). And `s[2]` reads at `end+1` which is 1 byte past the buffer. So that's a READ of 1 byte past.

