```

Here `addr` is `g_strndup(start+1, length-2)`. So `addr` has `length-2` chars + nul. If `pct` points to the last char (position `length-3`), then `pct[1]='\0'`, `pct[2]` reads 1 past, `pct[3]` reads 2 past. That's a READ of 2 bytes past.

